1
00:00:05,690 --> 00:00:08,360
Hey, did you know
that three dates with the same woman...

2
00:00:08,526 --> 00:00:10,566
(Howard:)...is the threshold for sex?

3
00:00:11,362 --> 00:00:14,402
(Raj:)Actually, I've never had three dates
with the same woman.

4
00:00:14,615 --> 00:00:16,615
(Leonard:)With Penny and me, it took two years.

5
00:00:16,826 --> 00:00:21,036
But now that I think about it,
that was three dates.

6
00:00:21,706 --> 00:00:23,876
(Howard:)Okay, well,
before you and Penny hooked up...

7
00:00:24,041 --> 00:00:26,291
(Howard:)...did she ask
for any kind of commitment?

8
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:31,210
(Leonard:)No, she was pretty clear
about wanting to keep her options open.

9
00:00:31,716 --> 00:00:35,096
(Sheldon(arriving):)I have something to announce,
but out of respect for convention...

10
00:00:35,261 --> 00:00:37,931
(Sheldon(arriving):)...I will wait for you
to finish your conversation.

11
00:00:38,097 --> 00:00:39,557
(Sheldon(arriving):)What are you talking about?

12
00:00:39,724 --> 00:00:42,974
(Leonard:)The cultural paradigm in which
people have sex after three dates.

13
00:00:43,144 --> 00:00:44,224
(Sheldon:)I see.

14
00:00:44,395 --> 00:00:46,895
Now, are we talking "date"
the social interaction...

15
00:00:47,064 --> 00:00:49,774
...or "date" the dried fruit?

16
00:00:51,277 --> 00:00:53,067
(Howard:)Never mind.
What's your announcement?

17
00:00:53,237 --> 00:00:54,317
SHELDON:
Oh, good, my turn.

18
00:00:54,488 --> 00:00:58,238
(Sheldon:)Well, this is very exciting, and I wanted
you to be among the first to know--

19
00:00:58,409 --> 00:01:00,239
I hear you're gonna be on the radio...

20
00:01:00,411 --> 00:01:03,251
...with Ira Flatow from Science Friday
next week.

